avor, and with years in bottle it turns waxy, honeyed and Burgundian.","x":"284:2,285:75,286:3,287:55,288:60,289:68,290:78,291:12,292:0,293:30,202:75,34:50,47:45,49:45,51:25,69:20,100:40,79:35,73:30,116:25,104:20,193:30,192:20,141:55,136:50,222:45,224:35,230:40,236:65,248:65,243:65,258:70,260:60,282:85,280:45,303:100,305:100,298:100,312:100"},{"s":"bartolo-mascarello-barolo","n":"Barolo","p":"Bartolo Mascarello","t":"red","c":"Italy","r":"Piedmont","a":"Barolo DOCG","g":["Nebbiolo"],"pr":250,"abv":14.5,"e":"Long traditional maceration, about three years in large Slavonian oak botti","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2–3 hours","w":"10–40 years from vintage","ds":"The standard-bearer of traditional Barolo, blended from several crus: sour cherry, rose and tar with licorice, truffle and dried orange peel. Severe and tight in youth, it unfurls over decades into something ethereal and endlessly complex.","x":"284:2,285:82,286:90,287:68,288:68,289:80,290:92,291:20,292:0,293:35,2:80,1:45,26:40,39:25,72:85,197:45,71:30,198:80,126:45,111:30,114:30,99:15,124:15,150:40,148:35,185:30,186:30,143:25,216:70,214:55,217:35,239:60,258:100,248:90,245:90,254:40,252:75,260:85,282:100,279:40,297:100,310:100,294:100,315:100,299:100"},{"s":"paolo-scavino-bric-del-fiasc-barolo","n":"Bric del Fiasc Barolo","p":"Paolo Scavino","t":"red","c":"Italy","r":"Piedmont","a":"Barolo DOCG","g":["Nebbiolo"],"pr":140,"abv":14.5,"e":"About 10 months in French barriques, then more than a year in large oak casks","sv":"16–18°C","d":"2 hours","w":"8–30 years from vintage","ds":"Modern-school Barolo from Castiglione Falletto: deeper, darker fruit than the traditionalists, with black cherry, violet and tar polished by a touch of cocoa and toast. Dense, powerful tannins are fine-grained and glossy, built for the long haul.","x":"284:3,285:75,286:85,287:70,288:80,289:85,290:88,291:45,292:0,293:30,14:60,2:60,1:35,15:30,72:60,71:55,198:60,126:50,99:20,111:15,170:35,156:25,157:25,164:15,142:30,143:25,148:15,219:60,214:55,216:45