","a":"Rueda DO","g":["Verdejo"],"pr":18,"abv":13,"e":"Stainless steel with lees ageing","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–3 years","ds":"Rueda Verdejo at its most expressive: lime, grapefruit and green pear with fennel, cut grass and the variety''s signature bitter-almond finish. Crisp and fleshy at once, a natural partner for tapas and anything fried.","x":"284:3,285:75,286:0,287:45,288:42,289:65,290:55,291:0,292:0,293:8,35:60,36:60,34:40,46:45,49:40,53:30,60:20,68:35,66:25,100:50,89:40,85:30,202:45,136:25,228:65,229:50,224:20,240:85,256:60,252:40,266:25,261:85,279:85,283:70,319:100,305:100,313:100,318:100,323:100"},{"s":"ameztoi-getariako-txakolina-blanco","n":"Getariako Txakolina Blanco","p":"Ameztoi","t":"white","c":"Spain","r":"Basque Country","a":"Getariako Txakolina DO","g":["Hondarrabi Zuri"],"pr":22,"abv":11,"e":"Stainless steel; bottled with natural CO2 retained","sv":"6–8°C","d":"Not needed; pour from height","w":"Drink within 2 years","ds":"Sea air in a bottle: tart lemon, green apple and white grapefruit with a saline, almost briny snap and a prickle of natural CO2. Low in alcohol and high in tension, it is built for the pintxo bar and the beach.","x":"284:2,285:92,286:0,287:20,288:25,289:55,290:50,291:0,292:15,293:5,34:70,35:50,40:40,46:65,36:40,69:25,85:20,89:25,141:80,144:40,136:45,235:75,228:85,225:60,230:50,240:95,243:55,256:60,261:85,279:90,283:85,306:100,305:100,303:100,323:100"},{"s":"juve-y-camps-reserva-de-la-familia-brut-nature","n":"Reserva de la Familia Brut Nature Gran Reserva","p":"Juvé & Camps","t":"sparkling","c":"Spain","r":"Penedès","a":"Cava DO","g":["Xarel·lo","Macabeo","Parellada"],"pr":25,"abv":12,"e":"Traditional method; about 36 months on lees, zero dosage","sv":"6–8°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Now–5 years","ds":"Proof that great Cava need not be sweetened: green apple, lemon and fennel over toasted almond and brioche from three years on the lees. Bone-dry, chalky and fine-beaded, it''s an aperitif with real gastronomic backbone.","x":"284:2,285:80,286:0,287:38,288:45,289:62,290:68,291:0,292:95,293:35,46:60,47:35,34:55,40:35,49:35,51:20,85:25,100:30,111:15,202:50,203:25,178:50,184:45,180:35,181:30,138:45,136:35,141:25,233:70,228:70,225:35,240:75,249:50,258:60,272:95,266:50,280:50,323:100,319:100,301:100,305:100,307:100"},{"s":"bodegas-borsao-tres-picos-garnacha","n":"Tres Picos Garnacha","p":"Bodegas Borsao","t":"red","c":"Spain","r":"Aragón","a":"Campo de Borja DO","g":["Garnacha"],"pr":20,"abv":15,"e":"About 5 months in French oak barrels","sv":"15–17°C","d":"30 minutes","w":"Now–6 years","ds":"Old-vine Garnacha from the foothills of the Moncayo, ripe and unabashed: kirsch, raspberry jam and blackberry with licorice, garrigue and a dusting of cocoa. Plush and warm with soft tannins, it overdelivers wildly for the money.","x":"284:5,285:48,286:45,287:82,288:75,289:78,290:62,291:30,292:0,293:20,3:65,27:60,28:55,12:50,14:50,9:35,4:25,126:45,106:40,120:25,135:30,170:30,156:25,157:20,153:25,226:65,213:50,224:45,241:85,244:80,250:70,256:75,257:40,278:55,279:65,300:100,302:100,296:100,309:100,311:100"},{"s":"gonzalez-byass-tio-pepe-fino","n":"Tío Pepe Fino","p":"González Byass","t":"fortified","c":"Spain","r":"Andalucía","a":"Jerez-Xérès-Sherry DO","g":["Palomino"],"pr":20,"abv":15,"e":"Biological ageing under flor for about four years in a solera of American oak butts","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Drink fresh; finish within a week or two of opening (refrigerate)","ds":"The world''s reference Fino: bready flor, green almond and chamomile over a bone-dry, saline palate. Light-footed yet piercing, it snaps the appetite awake and turns olives, jamón and fried fish into a feast.","x":"284:0,285:55,286:2,287:88,288:35,289:72,290:70,291:15,292:0,293:40,207:95,202:80,141:75,113:35,79:40,116:30,179:45,181:40,46:25,40:30,138:40,136:25,196:30,228:60,225:55,230:40,240:75,242:85,258:95,249:50,275:85,276:85,260:60,283:70,323:100,301:100,319:100,305:100,307:100"},{"s":"bodegas-hidalgo-la-gitana-manzanilla","n":"La Gitana Manzanilla","p":"Bodegas Hidalgo-La Gitana","t":"fortified","c":"Spain","r":"Andalucía","a":"Manzanilla-Sanlúcar de Barrameda DO","g":["Palomino"],"pr":16,"abv":15,"e":"Biological ageing under thick Sanlúcar flor, roughly 4–5 years in solera; also common in 375ml half-bottles","sv":"7–9°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Drink fresh; refrigerate and finish soon after opening","ds":"Sanlúcar''s sea breeze in liquid form: chamomile, green apple and fresh bread over a tangy, salty, almost briny finish. Lighter and more delicate than Fino, it is the definitive partner for fried seafood and shellfish.","x":"284:0,285:58,286:2,287:88,288:30,289:65,290:65,291:12,292:0,293:35,207:90,141:90,202:65,79:50,46:35,40:35,179:40,181:35,113:30,144:35,138:35,116:25,196:25,228:65,225:60,240:85,242:80,254:40,258:90,275:85,276:85,260:60,283:75,305:100,319:100,306:100,323:100,301:100"},{"s":"lustau-los-arcos-dry-amontillado","n":"Los Arcos Dry Amontillado (Solera Reserva)","p":"Emilio Lustau","t":"fortified","c":"Spain","r":"Andalucía","a":"Jerez-Xérès-Sherry DO","g":["Palomino"],"pr":20,"abv":18.5,"e":"Begins under flor, then fortified and aged oxidatively in a solera of American oak butts; average age around 8 years","sv":"12–14°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Stable on release; keeps several weeks once opened","ds":"Two lives in one glass: the saline, almond-skin tang of flor overlaid with roasted hazelnut, toffee and dried orange from years of oxidative ageing. Dry, tangy and endlessly savoury, it''s superb with consommé, mushrooms and aged cheese.","x":"284:2,285:58,286:3,287:92,288:55,289:80,290:85,291:30,292:0,293:75,203:85,202:60,204:45,206:40,171:25,207:45,141:60,39:40,32:25,186:30,185:15,196:40,195:15,211:20,125:20,208:30,156:10,223:25,230:30,242:85,248:80,258:85,275:95,276:90,267:70,260:60,281:75,310:100,315:100,301:100,298:100"},{"s":"gonzalez-byass-alfonso-oloroso-seco","n":"Alfonso Oloroso Seco","p":"González Byass","t":"fortified","c":"Spain","r":"Andalucía","a":"Jerez-Xérès-Sherry DO","g":["Palomino"],"pr":22,"abv":18,"e":"Fortified to about 18% so flor cannot form; purely oxidative ageing in an American oak solera for around 8 years","sv":"13–15°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Stable on release; keeps weeks once opened","ds":"Dry Oloroso, broad and burnished: walnut, toffee and dried fig with a polished, almost leathery depth and no sweetness at all. Its weight and tang make it a revelation with stews, game and hard cheese.","x":"284:3,285:52,286:4,287:92,288:72,289:82,290:85,291:38,292:0,293:80,204:85,203:55,202:30,206:55,171:40,22:40,24:25,25:20,39:35,185:40,186:35,159:20,123:25,125:25,196:35,208:40,141:30,223:40,224:50,242:80,248:75,237:50,258:80,275:95,276:90,267:95,260:60,281:80,297:100,315:100,310:100,296:100"},{"s":"lustau-san-emilio-pedro-ximenez","n":"San Emilio Pedro Ximénez (Solera Reserva)","p":"Emilio Lustau","t":"fortified","c":"Spain","r":"Andalucía","a":"Jerez-Xérès-Sherry DO","g":["Pedro Ximénez"],"pr":30,"abv":17,"e":"Sun-dried grapes; fortified must aged in an American oak solera, averaging roughly 8–12 years","sv":"12–14°C","d":"Not needed","w":"Virtually indestructible; keeps months once opened","ds":"Liquid raisin-and-date confection, black as molasses: fig, prune, coffee and licorice flow over an unctuous, syrupy palate. Pour it over vanilla ice cream or alongside blue cheese and dark chocolate.","x":"284:100,285:35,286:3,287:90,288:100,289:95,290:90,291:30,292:0,293:75,24:95,25:85,22:80,23:70,30:40,173:65,174:45,171:40,206:35,166:45,168:35,126:35,204:30,124:25,123:20,199:20,223:90,226:60,238:85,257:90,255:90,275:95,276:85,271:60,281:65,321:100,317:100,320:100"},{"s":"quinta-do-crasto-reserva-old-vines","n":"Reserva Old Vines","p":"Quinta do Crasto","t":"red","c":"Portugal","r":"Douro","a":"Douro DOC","g":["Touriga Nacional","Tinta Roriz","Touriga Franca","Tinta Barroca","Old-vine field blend"],"pr":45,"abv":14.5,"e":"16–18 months in French and American oak barrels","sv":"16–18°C","d":"1 hour","w":"3–15 years 